          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mb-2">2. The 8-Hour Sleep Rule</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
              In a landmark clinical study published in the <em>Annals of Internal Medicine</em>, researchers found that sleeping 5.5 hours versus 8.5 hours shifted nutrient partitioning drastically: the sleep-deprived group lost <strong>60% more muscle tissue and stored more body fat</strong> under identical caloric conditions. Sleep is when human growth hormone (HGH) peaks and muscle tissue repair takes place. Prioritize 7 to 9 hours nightly.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
